%description:

Tcp.dropSynData:drop -- the data of a SYN is dropped, and the client sends it again.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "the data of a SYN that Fast Open does not accept is dropped, so the
SYN-ACK acknowledges only the SYN and the client sends the data again, as Linux".

The classes: keep (false, the default), drop (true; LinuxTcp). The code: the text of a SYN that
Fast Open does not accept waits in the receive queue, and the ACK that ends the handshake
processes it (TcpConnection::processSegmentInSynRcvd()), or it is dropped
(processSegmentInListen()). The client sends the data again with the ACK of the SYN-ACK in
both classes, because the SYN-ACK acknowledges only the SYN; so the tap removes that data, and
only the queue of host2 can hold it. This test separates "drop" from "keep", with which
host2 acknowledges the 500 bytes at once.

Host under test: host2, the server, without Fast Open. Peer: host1 sends 500 bytes on its SYN,
without a cookie. Observation: level 1, host2 acknowledges the 500 bytes only after host1
sends them again, after its retransmission timeout of 1 s.

%# parameter: Tcp.dropSynData
%# class: drop
%# value: true
%# key: *.host2.tcp.dropSynData
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"
#include "TcpMutations.h"
#include "TcpTestApp.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpDropSynDataDrop")
        .intercept(tap("tap").from("host1").filterPacket("tcp.synBit == false && ipv4.totalLengthField > 100B").nth(1)
                     .mutate([](Packet *frame) { removeTcpData(frame); })
                     .describe("the data that host1 sends again with the ACK of the SYN-ACK (remove it)"))
        .act(action().at(0.1).run<TcpTestApp>("host1.app[0]", [](TcpTestApp& app) {
            app.socket().connect(app.addressOf("host2"), 1000, true);
            app.sendData(app.socket(), 500);
        }))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
                  .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && pk.dataLength > tcp.headerLength")
                  .capture("isn", "tcp.sequenceNo")
                  .describe("the SYN of host1, with 500 bytes and without a cookie")
                  .within(0.5))
        .never(on("host2.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
                   .filterPacket("tcp.ackBit == true && tcp.synBit == false && tcp.ackNo == {isn} + 501")
                   .describe("an ACK of host2 for the 500 bytes before host1 sends them again")
                   .within(0.8))
        .once(on("host2.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
                  .filterPacket("tcp.ackBit == true && tcp.synBit == false && tcp.ackNo == {isn} + 501")
                  .describe("the ACK of host2 for the 500 bytes, after host1 sends them again")
                  .within(2.0));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpDropSynDataDrop compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host2.tcp.dropSynData = true    # the parameter under test
*.host1.app[0].typename = "TcpTestApp"
*.host1.tcp.fastopenClientEnabled = true
*.host1.tcp.fastopenClientNoCookieRequired = true
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpDropSynDataDrop: PASS
